  "title": "Census 6 depends on how it is glued",
  "status": "Proved",
  "claim": "Census 6 depends on how it is glued (proved by exhaustive symmetry computation; measured). The creation test splits each far side at a point and glues the i-th line through it to the i-th listed point of the gluing line. The signed symmetries fixing that point permute its three lines in all six ways for K4^(3), the Fano plane and census 58, so their verdicts do not depend on that order; for census 6 only two, so it has three inequivalent gluings. Measured on every third saved space (11,552 non-degenerate pairs): K4^(3), the Fano plane, census 58 and whether creation occurs never change with the order; census 6 changes in 8,046 pairs, creating at none, exactly one or all three of its gluings. In the Fano plane alone census 6 creates at 14 of the 42 ordered pairs in the stored orders, but natively at one gluing of three at every pair. Census 58 is split at a point of its two-point orbit. The native repair counts census 6's gluings that create.",
